---
import Answer from "../../components/challenge/Answer.astro";
import ChallengeIntro from "../../components/challenge/ChallengeIntro.astro";
import Checklist from "../../components/challenge/Checklist.astro";
import Message from "../../components/challenge/Message.astro";
import Task from "../../components/challenge/Task.astro";
import PageShell from "../../components/PageShell.astro";
import MainLayout from "../../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
---

<MainLayout title="Convert Content - AI Training Guide">
	<PageShell chapterId="exploring-ai-capabilities" subChapterId="convert-content">
		<ChallengeIntro skill="You can hand the agent a messy Word document of content changes and have it apply them, asking about the ones it can't act on instead of guessing.">
			The CEO sent the web team a Word document of changes to the public website. It's about two and a half pages, and some
			requests are clearer than others.
		</ChallengeIntro>

		<Message
			kind="email"
			subject="Website changes"
			from="CEO"
			to="Web Team"
			date="Mon, 28 Sep 2026 07:15"
			attachments={[{ name: "ceo-website-changes.docx", href: "/downloads/kaiju-mutual/16.ceo-website-changes.docx" }]}
		>
			<p>Team, changes for the website are attached. I'm travelling until Thursday, so just use your judgement.</p>
		</Message>

		<Task>Write a prompt to have your agent apply the CEO's changes to the website, and ask you about anything it shouldn't guess.</Task>

		<Checklist
			items={[
				"Read the whole document, including anything buried in tables, highlights or the sign-off.",
				"Make the changes that are clear.",
				"Ask you about every request that is vague, missing information or contradicts something else, and invent an answer for none of them.",
				"Point out anything that would make the site wrong or inconsistent, instead of changing it silently.",
				"Check each change in the browser.",
				"Give you a short list for the CEO: what was done, what's waiting on them, and why.",
			]}
		/>

		<Answer
			prompt={`Make the changes the CEO is asking for in this document: <attached document>.

Go through it request by request. Make the ones that are clear. For anything vague, missing information, contradicting another request or the rest of the site, or that would make something on the site wrong, don't guess: list it and ask me. "Use your judgement" isn't permission to fill in the gaps.

Check the changes in the browser, then give me a short list for the CEO: what was done, what's waiting on them, and why.`}
		>
			<p>Requests worth checking how the agent handled:</p>
			<ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
				<li>
					<strong>"Household is from $45 now":</strong> the price comes from the API's rating engine, not the copy. Changing only
					the site would promise $45 and quote $48. A good agent says so and asks whether to change the engine too.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>"Update everywhere it says 48":</strong> this means the two "48 hours" assessor lines. A find and replace on
					"48" also hits the $48 price.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>The "Our Leader" bio, "as is":</strong> it says the CEO founded the company in 1994, when the site says 40
					businesses founded it in 1961 and the policyholders own it. It also claims eleven events instead of 212. A good agent
					pastes nothing it knows is false and raises the clashes.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Requests with nothing to act on:</strong> the business price "like we discussed", "more exciting" plans, "move
					the thing about shelters up", a Careers link with no page, and a headshot that isn't attached. Each one needs a question.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Conflicts:</strong> a second headline that contradicts the first, and "don't change the claims page except the
					bold thing" when the 24-hour change also lands there.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Push back:</strong> "make it funnier, maybe some emojis" goes against the site's straight-faced tone. The
					struck-through chatbot is canceled, so it shouldn't be built.
				</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				The footer phone number is findable: the consumer portal already shows the real hotline. Gold isn't in the palette, so the
				pull quote should use the closest color token, and the agent should say so.
			</p>
		</Answer>
	</PageShell>
</MainLayout>
